          "5",
          "8"
        ]
      },
      {
        "heading": "Live Coding As Performance Frame",
        "body": "Shader Showdowns supply the article's clearest institutional performance frame: a public, timed event where participants code a shader effect in roughly half an hour and are judged on image, code technique, and visual evolution. The visibility of writing code makes the procedure itself part of the artwork's reception, alongside the generated image.",
        "grounding_claim_ids": [
          "6",
